course: dictionary
lesson: 13780
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Intoxicated is a formal word, so you may meet it in the news, in law, or in a story. It has two meanings. The first is drunk, or affected by drugs, so that you cannot think or act normally. «The man was intoxicated, so the police would not let him drive.» The clue is that he could not drive safely, so intoxicated must mean drunk.
explain: The second meaning is very excited and happy, as if you were drunk. «She was intoxicated with joy when she won the race.» Here nobody has had a drink. The clue is joy: she was so happy that she felt light-headed.
explain: Always check the words around the word. If the sentence is about driving, danger or the police, the meaning is usually drunk. If it is about winning, joy or success, the meaning is usually very happy and excited.
fact: Intoxicated is an adjective: «He was intoxicated.» It comes from the verb intoxicate, which has the form intoxicated in the past.
fact: «Intoxicated» means drunk, or affected by drugs, so that you cannot think or act normally.
fact: «Intoxicated with joy» means so happy and excited that you feel as if you were drunk.
fact: Driving while intoxicated is a crime, and it is very dangerous for the driver and everyone else on the road.
fact: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. If «drunk» or «very happy» still makes sense in the sentence, you have found the right meaning.
exercise: «The driver was intoxicated, so he was not allowed on the road.» What does intoxicated mean here? | Very tired after a long day | Lost on the road | Very excited about a race | *Drunk, so he could not think or act safely
exercise: «The children were intoxicated with joy when the snow began to fall.» What does intoxicated suggest? | *So excited and happy that they felt as if they were drunk | Cold and wet | Angry and cross | Sleepy after lunch
exercise: Ruby says driving while intoxicated is a crime. Why is it a crime? | Because the road is too narrow | *Because a person who is intoxicated cannot think or act normally, so driving is dangerous | Because it rains a lot in winter | Because cars are too expensive
test: «After three drinks, he was intoxicated and could not stand up straight.» Which word best matches intoxicated? | Alert and calm | *Drunk | Bored | Hungry
test: «He was intoxicated by success after winning the medal.» What does intoxicated mean here? | Very sad | Very tired | Cold and hungry | *Very excited and happy
exam: A police officer says, «The driver was intoxicated.» What does intoxicated mean? | Late for work | *Drunk, or affected by drugs | Excited about the drive | Lost on the way
